232.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15450003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Garg, S., J. Narula, and Y. Chandrashekhar. <year>2005</year>. Apoptosis and heart failure: clinical relevance and therapeutic target. <source>J. Mol. Cell. Cardiol.</source> <volume>38</volume>:<fpage>73</fpage>&#x02013;79.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15623423</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Gill, C., R. Mestril, and A. Samali. <year>2002</year>. Losing heart: the role of apoptosis in heart disease&#x02014;a novel therapeutic target? <source>FASEB J.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>135</fpage>&#x02013;146.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11818361</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Harlin, H., S.B. Reffey, C.S. Duckett, T. Lindsten, and C.B. Thompson. <year>2001</year>. Characterization of XIAP-deficient mice. <source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>3604</fpage>&#x02013;3608.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11313486</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Hengartner, M.O. <year>2000</year>. The biochemistry of apoptosis. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>407</volume>:<fpage>770</fpage>&#x02013;776.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11048727</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Hu, Y., M.A. Benedict, L. Ding, and G. Nunez. <year>1999</year>. Role of cytochrome c and dATP/ATP hydrolysis in Apaf-1-mediated caspase-9 activation and apoptosis. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>18</volume>:<fpage>3586</fpage>&#x02013;3595.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10393175</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Juin, P., A.O. Hueber, T. Littlewood, and G. Evan. <year>1999</year>. c-Myc-induced sensitization to apoptosis is mediated through cytochrome <italic>c</italic> release. <source>Genes Dev.</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>1367</fpage>&#x02013;1381.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10364155</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Kluck, R.M., W.E. Bossy, D.R. Green, and D.D. Newmeyer. <year>1997</year>. The release of cytochrome c from mitochondria: a primary site for Bcl-2 regulation of apoptosis. <source>Science.</source> <volume>275</volume>:<fpage>1132</fpage>&#x02013;1136.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9027315</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Li, F., A. Srinivasan, Y. Wang, R.C. Armstrong, K.J. Tomaselli, and L.C. Fritz. <year>1997</year>. Cell-specific induction of apoptosis by microinjection of cytochrome <italic>c</italic>. Bcl-XL has activity independent of cytochrome <italic>c</italic> release. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>272</volume>:<fpage>30299</fpage>&#x02013;30305.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9374516</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Liu, X., C.N. Kim, J. Yang, R. Jemmerson, and X. Wang. <year>1996</year>. Induction of apoptotic program in cell-free extracts: requirement for dATP and cytochrome c. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>86</volume>:<fpage>147</fpage>&#x02013;157.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8689682</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Moroni, M.C., E.S. Hickman, E.L. Denchi, G. Caprara, E. Colli, F. Cecconi, H. Muller, and K. Helin. <year>2001</year>. Apaf-1 is a transcriptional target for E2F and p53. <source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>552</fpage>&#x02013;558.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11389439</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Narula, J., P. Pandey, E. Arbustini, N. Haider, N. Narula, F.D. Kolodgie, B.B. Dal, M.J. Semigran, M.A. Bielsa, G.W. Dec, et al. <year>1999</year>. Apoptosis in heart failure: release of cytochrome <italic>c</italic> from mitochondria and activation of caspase-3 in human cardiomyopathy. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>96</volume>:<fpage>8144</fpage>&#x0201